# Git LFS — large binary assets are stored out-of-band, with a small text
# pointer committed in their place. Requires `git-lfs`; see the "Checking out
# the repository" section in README.md.
#
# `filter=lfs` routes the file through the LFS clean/smudge filters,
# `diff=lfs` and `merge=lfs` keep Git from trying to text-diff or merge it,
# and `-text` disables end-of-line translation on a binary file.

*.mp4 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
